  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "T21-2e: the implicit `any \\ error` contract of an untyped pn parameter only rejects an error Item. A closed `+ - *` int tree over int-lane leaves (element reads with an int witness and int keys, counter locals, literals) has no error arm -- overflow widens on the checked slow arm and an out-of-range read yields the lane null -- so the call-site lambda_type_check on such an argument is redundant and is elided (levenshtein paid it three times per inner iteration for its min3 arguments). Both calls in main pass only such trees.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_main_#",
      "forbid": [
        "call\tlambda_type_check_p, lambda_type_check"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
